## Vercel upload exclusions. The main clone carries local research/extraction
## material that must never ship: mirror .gitignore here (Vercel does not read
## .gitignore) so deploys from this folder upload only the application.
##
## Anchor every repo-root entry with a leading slash. Unanchored names match at
## ANY depth, which is how `supabase/` silently dropped web/vendor/supabase/ and
## broke same-origin sign-in in production. Only the patterns that are genuinely
## meant to match anywhere stay unanchored: node_modules, .NET bin/obj, secrets,
## logs, and `fixtures/` (which must keep catching scripts/tests/fixtures).
/.git
node_modules/
bin/
obj/
src/**/bin/
src/**/obj/
*.log
*.pid
.env
.env.local
.env.example
/out/
/tools/
/supabase/
/.wrangler/
/.bench/
/.agents/
/.codex/
/.claude/
/Output/
/design-handoff/
/data-build-baselines/
/data-build-receipts/
fixtures/
/local-adviser/
/plans/
/as.json
/cm.json
/pp.json
/r2.json
/reddit_post.json
/post_body.md
/post_text.txt
/aes.txt
/oodle-data-shared.dll
/zlib-ng2.dll
/extraction-report.md
/mastery-node-images.md
/FIX-PLAN.md
